<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saloninus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 260</span> · Also known as Publius Licinius Cornelius Saloninus Valerianus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saloninus was the younger son of the Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallienus">Gallienus</a>. Left at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> as Caesar under the guardianship of the prefect Silvanus, he was proclaimed Augustus in 260 when the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/postumus">Postumus</a> revolted. Postumus besieged the city, and the garrison handed over Saloninus and Silvanus, who were put to death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saloninus.jpg" alt="Saloninus" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cng · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoninianus_of_Saloninus_Caesar_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
